# staging-plane.register — the EXACT set of surviving staging-plane references in the
# executable/configuration corpus, as adjudicated by FOLLOW-878 (ESC-052 RESOLVED,
# CEO option 2). Enforced by scripts/check-no-staging-plane.sh (hard gate in ci.yml).
#
# Format: <pattern> TAB <path> TAB <count>.  A NEW line = a new reference to a plane
# that does not exist (FAIL).  A VANISHED line = the reference was removed (also FAIL,
# so the register cannot rot) — update this file in the same PR that removes it.
#
# REASON FOR EVERY SURVIVING LINE
# -------------------------------
# .github/workflows/db-migrate.yml  (--config stg, DOPPLER_TOKEN_STG)
#     OWNED BY FOLLOW-873, deliberately NOT touched by FOLLOW-878 (its AC(4): do not
#     do that ticket's work twice).  This is the non-protective staging->prod gate
#     ESC-052 exposed — `stg` is byte-identical to `prd`, so every merged migration
#     has been applied to production twice.  When FOLLOW-873 collapses it to a single
#     prod apply, these two lines disappear and this gate goes RED until the register
#     is updated.  That is the intended handoff, not a defect.
# .github/workflows/deploy-staging.yml  (--env staging, [env.staging], ingest hostname)
#     The BUNDLE/UPLOAD SMOKE.  Kept deliberately (FOLLOW-810): it injects no Doppler
#     secrets, touches no data plane, is workflow_dispatch-only, and its header says
#     exactly what it is.  The hostname mentions are inside that explanatory header.
# apps/ingest/wrangler.toml  ([env.staging], hostnames)
#     The upload-smoke target.  The block carries the FOLLOW-878 correction
#     comment (no DNS record, no KV/DO/queue bindings, nothing auto-deploys).
#     (The Decision API Worker's wrangler.toml, its upload job and its staging
#     hostname lines left this register 2026-09-24 when FOLLOW-1262 removed it.)
# .github/workflows/load-test.yml  (INGEST_STAGING_URL, ingest-staging.estalara.com)
#     Mentions inside the FOLLOW-878 correction comment recording WHY the `staging`
#     target was removed.  No code path reads either token any more.
# packages/shared/src/domains.ts  (the two remaining *-staging.estalara.com literals)
#     Dead exports — zero consumers repo-wide — describing hosts with no DNS record.
#     Annotated in place; deletion is filed as FOLLOW-896.
# infra/terraform/cloudflare/workers.tf  (--env staging)
#     A comment describing the upload smoke, corrected by FOLLOW-878.
--config stg	.github/workflows/db-migrate.yml	2
[env.staging]	.github/workflows/deploy-staging.yml	1
[env.staging]	apps/ingest/wrangler.toml	1
--env staging	.github/workflows/deploy-staging.yml	1
--env staging	infra/terraform/cloudflare/workers.tf	1
DOPPLER_TOKEN_STG	.github/workflows/db-migrate.yml	6
INGEST_STAGING_URL	.github/workflows/load-test.yml	1
ingest-staging.estalara.com	.github/workflows/deploy-staging.yml	1
ingest-staging.estalara.com	.github/workflows/load-test.yml	1
ingest-staging.estalara.com	apps/ingest/wrangler.toml	2
ingest-staging.estalara.com	packages/shared/src/domains.ts	2
cdn-staging.estalara.com	packages/shared/src/domains.ts	1
